# The build context is the repository root, so everything below would otherwise
# be shipped to the daemon on every build - and some of it would end up in an
# image.

# Reinstalled inside the image, and a host's copy is the wrong platform anyway:
# argon2 is a native module built against the machine that installed it.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own; copying a stale one in is how a
# container ends up serving yesterday's code.
dist
**/dist
**/dist-worker
**/.next
tmp

# Local caches. Large, machine-specific, and meaningless in a container.
.nx
.git
**/.turbo

# Secrets. The API's .env holds a Gemini key and database credentials, and
# nothing in an image should ever have read them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Documentation and local-only infrastructure.
**/*.md
docker-compose.yml
